Package: stamp
Version: 1.0.2
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Maintainer: Stamp Maintainers <noreply@example.org>
Depends: python3 (>= 3.10), python3-gi, gir1.2-gtk-4.0, gir1.2-adw-1, gir1.2-udisks-2.0, pkexec | policykit-1, polkitd | policykit-1, udisks2, parted, dosfstools, rsync, util-linux
Description: Format an SD card as FAT32 (any size) and load a zip's contents onto it
 Stamp formats a removable SD card or USB drive as FAT32, explicitly
 supporting cards larger than 32GB (which most stock GUI formatters
 refuse or cap), and copies the contents of a user-provided zip file
 onto it.
 .
 Includes a GTK4/libadwaita GUI and a `stamp --cli` scripting mode that
 share the same core logic. Formatting requires one-time PolicyKit
 authentication for a small, auditable privileged helper that does
 nothing but partition + mkfs.vfat -F 32 the selected device.
